st fairness, oversized requests, and cancellation ordering. (semaphore/semaphore_test.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Scoped Sensei preflight classifies the one-file change as LOW_RISK with local blast radius and no approval gate, but confidence is low because no anchored rule governs the request. (semaphore/semaphore.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei associates a candidate public API contract with semaphore/semaphore.go, but no active file-level invariant was verified. (contract:contract.library_api.semaphore) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: bounded-knowledge-gap\n"}
